From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:21:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: Publish the display cadence from fence
 deadlines

macOS publishes the display's frame period to region C, +0x988 holding
a vblank and +0x990 the period, both in 24 MHz counter ticks, with the
period between 100,000 and 400,000, then sends control message 0x22 so
the firmware rereads them. After boot, macOS 26.6.2 holds 399,997 there,
the 60 Hz panel.

A display commit that waits on a render fence gives it the next vblank
start as its deadline, and deadlines a frame apart give the period.
Publish them, before each publication pass, when the period changes or
the phase moves by more than 100 us. With no deadlines for half a
second, publish the shortest period: left at a display's period, the
firmware holds headless work back to it. display_cadence=0 turns this
off.

On the J713, on battery, against display_cadence=0:
- headless vkmark scores 7,315 to 7,537 at 8.3 W, against 6,250 to
  6,274 at 7.4 W, so 18 % faster and 5 % more work per joule;
- a vsync-bound shader at 60 FPS on the panel draws 3.80 W, against
  3.90 W (means of four runs);
- idle power is unchanged, 3.22 W;
- left at 60 Hz once the display stops, headless vkmark scores only
  3,571 to 3,770, which the shortest period avoids.

The cadence's layout and message are from interface notes by Ibrahim
Syed <ibrahim.syed787b@gmail.com>, written from macOS's GPU driver. With
400,000 published, the firmware's controller words on the J713 reach
macOS's values (bundle +0x5384 400000, +0x7f68 16666, +0x7f6c 2).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
